        ":question/problem": "Calculate the integral $\\int \\frac{7 \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let's set $u=\\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}.$ Then, we have\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{x^{3}}\\cdot 3 x^{2}=\\frac{3}{x}\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\frac{1}{3}\\text{d}u=\\frac{\\text{d}x}{x}.\n$$\n\nUsing the above, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{7 \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}}{x}\\,\\text{d}x & =7\\int \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}\\cdot \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =7\\int u\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\int u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{3}\\cdot \\frac{u^{2}}{2}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7 u^{2}}{6}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{7 \\ln{\\left(x^{3} \\right)}^{2}}{6}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
